WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:05.460
Sharpen your axes, because it's time to return&nbsp;
to the age of "Vikings." The second season of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:09.900
"Vikings: Valhalla" is cresting the horizon,&nbsp;
and we'd all better be prepared for its attack.

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:14.760
It seemed "Vikings" was at an end when the&nbsp;
original History series concluded in 2020.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:19.620
But it wasn't long before the show's creator,&nbsp;
Michael Hirst, passed the torch to Jeb Stuart,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:24.420
who crossed the streaming seas to Netflix&nbsp;
and gave us "Vikings: Valhalla," a sequel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:29.340
series set a century after the events of its&nbsp;
predecessor. "Valhalla" introduced fans to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:34.200
Prince Harald of Norway and hero-in-the-making&nbsp;
Leif Erikson. Initially wary of one another,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:37.920
the two became allies to change&nbsp;
the time of the Vikings forever.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:41.760
Of course, they've still got to overcome&nbsp;
some obstacles to get there. The first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:46.140
season ended with Leif seeing red and&nbsp;
Harald on the run after Kattegat's fall,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:49.799
so their combined comeback will need to be epic.

00:00:49.799 --> 00:00:52.491
"Freydis, it's over."

00:00:52.491 --> 00:00:57.000
Netflix offered up a first look at "Vikings:&nbsp;
Valhalla" Season 2 during the streamer's annual&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:01.680
TUDUM event. Starting shortly after the&nbsp;
events of the first season, Harald, Leif,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:06.300
and Freydis are on the run, only for Olaf to&nbsp;
push them back to the shoreline. Thankfully,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:12.420
help comes from above via an unknown ally. Is&nbsp;
Forkbeard fending for our heroes, or has his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:17.460
son King Canute turned up at the right time?&nbsp;
Whoever it is, they make an explosive impact.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:23.580
The second season will debut on January 12, 2023,&nbsp;
but Netflix hasn't released any other trailers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:27.600
keeping things close to the vest. The&nbsp;
first-season trailers hit only a few&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:31.740
short weeks before the season was released,&nbsp;
so the streamer seems to be taking that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:35.940
approach again. TUDUM did offer up this&nbsp;
brief synopsis of the season, though:

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:39.180
"Season 2 finds our heroes shortly&nbsp;
after the tragic fall of Kattegat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:42.360
an event that has shattered their&nbsp;
dreams and altered their destinies.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:45.720
Finding themselves suddenly&nbsp;
fugitives in Scandinavia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:50.820
they are forced to test their ambitions and&nbsp;
courage in worlds beyond their familiar fjords."

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:54.900
Showrunner Jeb Stuart further explained&nbsp;
to TUDUM that Harald and Leif will be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:58.140
traveling down the Dnieper River,&nbsp;
in an adventure he describes as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:01.980
similar to "Thelma and Louise," while&nbsp;
Freydís will be heading to the Baltic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:06.000
area of Pomerania. Stuart also promised&nbsp;
quite an array of characters, adding,

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.520
"We put together this motley crew of nobles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:12.420
Muslim astronomers and con men,&nbsp;
and they shove off from Novgorod."

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:16.500
Leo Suter and Sam Corlett will return to lay&nbsp;
waste to their enemies as Prince Harald and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:21.480
Leif Erikson, respectively, along with Frida&nbsp;
Gustavsson as Freydís Eiríksdóttir , Leif's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:25.440
sister. The latter has a crucial path of&nbsp;
her own as the last daughter of Uppsala.

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:30.660
Beyond that talented trifecta, the show will also&nbsp;
see the return of Jóhannes Haukur Jóhannesson&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:35.820
as the side-switching contender for the throne,&nbsp;
Olaf. Last seen threatening Kattegat and sending&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:40.140
its protectors running, Olaf's victory&nbsp;
was short-lived. King Canute's father,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:45.360
King Sweyn Forkbeard, approached with a fleet of&nbsp;
ships to bring down the treacherous tyrant. Expect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:50.280
all three to be returning for Season 2, along&nbsp;
with the surprise return of Caroline Henderson,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:55.260
who played Kattegat's fallen ruler, Jarl Haakon.&nbsp;
Speaking to Metro about her character's demise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:58.980
the Swedish star quipped about whether&nbsp;
she was totally gone from the series,

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:02.820
"We don't really know that. She might&nbsp;
turn up as a ghost or something."

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:07.080
If that's not enough, "Valhalla" will&nbsp;
also see the arrival of an MCU star&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:12.420
and a previous punching bag for boxing champ&nbsp;
Adonis Creed. Florian Munteanu of "Shang-Chi"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:16.200
and "Creed II" fame will play the part&nbsp;
of Byzantine general George Maniakes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:20.520
Bradley James of "Merlin" will play the&nbsp;
leader of a particularly pagan bunch of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:26.040
warriors. Hayat Kamille, Marcin Dorocinski,&nbsp;
and Sofya Lebedeva have also joined the cast.

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:30.780
In an interview with Digital Spy in&nbsp;
February 2022, Jeb Stuart revealed that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:34.560
even before the first season's release,&nbsp;
the second was well into development,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:38.940
and he was "dying to get it out there."&nbsp;
Even before swords were drawn for the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:44.520
season of "Valhalla," Netflix had given the&nbsp;
green light for a massive 24-episode order,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:49.201
assuring that we'd be seeing Leif and&nbsp;
Harald for at least three seasons. 

